  "text": "Recipe: Dahi Vada (Steamed)\nCreator: Nivedita Dogra Dubey\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: yellow mung dal, urad dal, soy yogurt, onion, fruit salt, ENO, roasted cumin powder, black salt, red chili powder, Tamarind Chutney\nCooking methods: soak, grind, whisk, steam, dip, no-cook\nInstructions: BATTER: Soak yellow mung dal for a couple of hours. Then grind it. Whisk the batter for few minutes till fluffy. Then add 1/2 tsp fruit salt. I added ENO.\nSTEAM: Steam in idli stand for 12 to 15 minutes. We can check with tip of knife \u2013 It should come off clean when poked into the steaming vada.\nHOT WATER SOAK: Dip the steamed vada in hot water for a few minutes, then drain. No need to squeeze out water. It doesn't soak much.\nSERVE: Add plant-based yogurt. Garnish with roasted cumin powder, black salt (if using salt), red chili powder and Tamarind Chutney.",
